Reason: nemsinterp wrote grid%smc (total soil water) into the sh2o records of the IC (output_nemsinit.F90 line 1773, the SH2O loop is a copy of the SMC loop), discarding the Flerchinger liquid/ice split that NMM_SH2O computes from STC+SMC. NMMB reads sh2o from the IC, so every cold start began with zero soil ice. Write grid%sh2o.
--- a/sorc/nam_nps.fd/sorc/NMMB_init/NPS/nemsinterp/src/output_nemsinit.F90	2026-11-06 06:15:41
+++ b/sorc/nam_nps.fd/sorc/NMMB_init/NPS/nemsinterp/src/output_nemsinit.F90	2026-11-06 06:15:47
@@ -1764,13 +1764,13 @@
          write(0,*) NCOUNT, ' SMC  '
        endif
 
-!--- SH2O SMC ----------------------------------------------------------
+!--- SH2O (liquid soil water; nam-recast patch nps-02: was grid%smc) --------
 
        do L=1,NSOIL
 
        do J=JTS,min(JTE,JDE_end)
        do I=ITS,min(ITE,IDE_end)
-         TEMP1(I,J)=grid%smc(I+ITARG,L,J+JTARG)
+         TEMP1(I,J)=grid%sh2o(I+ITARG,L,J+JTARG)
        enddo
        enddo
 
